Mutant: the start removes the last segment, or appends to it, before the removal of a leftover is synced. Must fail: a segment file without its index file is deleted as a leftover of cleanup, and the directory synced; a start syncs the removal of a leftover of cleanup before it removes the last segment.
Apply from the repository root with git apply, and never commit it applied.

--- a/src/bin/pgcopydb/ld_spool.c
+++ b/src/bin/pgcopydb/ld_spool.c
@@ -2356,7 +2356,7 @@
 
 	/* on disk before last goes, or a crash could leave it directly before the last */
 	if (start->leftover > 0 &&
-		(!unlink_file(leftover) || !spool_sync_directory(dirname)))
+		!unlink_file(leftover))
 	{
 		return false;
 	}
